, phorbol ester, elicits disparate functional responses in androgen-sensitive and androgen-independent human prostatic cancer cells</article-title><source>Biochem Biophyls Res Commun</source><year>1998</year><volume>244</volume><fpage>167</fpage><lpage>171</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Biochem Biophyls Res Commun||244|167||bib10|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Koivisto</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kononen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Palmberg</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Tammela</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hyytinen</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Isola</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Trapman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Cleutjens</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Noordzij</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Visakorpi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kallioniemi</surname><given-names>O-P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Androgen receptor gene amplification: a possible molecular mechanism for androgen deprivation therapy failure in prostate cancer</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1997</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>314</fpage><lpage>319</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||57|314||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9000575</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Koivisto</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Helin</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Androgen receptor gene amplification increases tissue PSA protein expression in hormone-refractory prostate carcinoma</article-title><source>J Pathol</source><year>1999</year><volume>189</volume><fpage>219</fpage><lpage>223</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Pathol||189|219||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10547578</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krishna</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Underwood</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Grigor</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bartlett</surname><given-names>JMS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>AP-1 as a mediator of androgen refractory prostate cancer</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2002</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>s34</fpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||86|s34||bib13|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>HK</given-names></name><name><surname>Yeh</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kang</surname><given-names>HY</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Akt suppresses androgen-induced apoptosis by phosphorylating and inhibiting androgen receptor</article-title><source>Proc Nat Acad Sci USA</source><year>2001</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>7200</fpage><lpage>7205</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Proc Nat Acad Sci USA||98|7200||bib14|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Latil</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Bieche</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Vidaud</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Lidereau</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Berthon</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><nam